#X obj 697 8 spring;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 216 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Smoothly moves the current value towards a target value
in a given time \, simulating the motion of a spring. The @accel property
controls the curve of the motion: 0 gives linear interpolation \, positive
values start fast and slow down near the target \, negative values
start slowly and accelerate towards the target.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Natural-feeling GUI behaviour — making knobs \, sliders
or number boxes return smoothly to a preset value after the user releases
the mouse \, instead of jumping instantly.;
#X text 50 342 Note: @mouse_events property is *on*;
